The University, founded in 1924, offers a wide range of degree programs at bachelor, master and doctoral levels as well as short vocational masters and specialization programs for each department.
Currently the University of Trieste has 10 departments: Economic; Business, Mathematical and Statistical Sciences; Engineering and Architecture; Humanities; Legal Studies; Languages; Interpreting and Translation Studies; Mathematics and Geosciences; Medicine; Surgery and Health Sciences; Life Studies; Pharmaceutical and Chemical Sciences; Physics; Political and Social Sciences. 
Research is encouraged in all fields of study.

There are 5 inter-department centers within the University:
- Inter-department center for Mind and Language studies;
- Inter-department center for Systems, Technologies and Services research;
- Inter-department center for European and Mediterranean studies;
- Inter-department center for Educational research;
- Inter-department center for Computational sciences.
Furthermore, the University has staff working in 14 different inter-university centers for research. 
These inter-university centers cover the Architecture and Engineering area, the Economical and Legal area, the Health area, the Scientific area and the Humanitarian and Linguistic area.

The University of Trieste participates in numerous national and international programs (H2020, InterReg, Erasmus Plus, Life…), investing the role of both partner and leader, and collaborates for these with many universities, in particular with ones from Eastern Europe and non-EU counties.

In 14-20 Programming Period, the number of projects with success is 23 and the total sum won by the University of Trieste is 6,484,243.75 €.

SYNPO was founded in 1952 as a state-owned Research Institute for Synthetic Resins and Coatings and it has been the leading center of applied R&D in polymers ever since.Since 1992 it is a "for-profit" company conducting: 
- Contract R&D and product development in synthetic polymers, coatings, composites, adhesives and polymers for electronic applications;
- Application development;
- Process development in SYNPO’s pilot plant and manufacturing facilities;
- Custom manufacturing and tolling;
- Analytical and testing services in accredited laboratories
- Training of PhD and MSc students in collaboration with the University of Pardubice
